WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 057. A FINISHED FILE HIDES ITS PRODUCTION HISTORY. Sources, people, tools, AI involvement, rights claims, edits, and exports can disappear behind one polished content object.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
REGISTER THE ARTIFACT. OBJECT · VERSION · TIME · RECORDER. Use an exact-bound synthetic artifact. Preserve identifiers, declared timestamps, recorders, source locators, transformations, tool events, people, AI claims, rights assertions, and missing links.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
PEEL IT BACKWARD. SOURCE · TRANSFORM · REVIEW · EXPORT. Move from the finished version toward each recorded input and event while the provenance graph and timeline stay synchronized.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
KEEP CLAIMS SEPARATE. RECORDED · LINKED · CORROBORATED · UNKNOWN. A record can show who asserted what and when. It cannot make an unverified source, identity, right, sequence, or AI-use claim true.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
BOUND THE RESULT. TRACE IS NOT VERIFICATION. The demo cannot conclude authorship, ownership, copyright, license, permission, authenticity, identity, completeness, chronology, admissibility, attribution, or AI detection.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. MAKE THE HISTORY INSPECTABLE. PROVENANCE BECOMES USEFUL WHEN EVERY VERSION, SOURCE, PERSON, TOOL, CLAIM, TRANSFORMATION, AND UNKNOWN CAN BE TRACED WITHOUT BECOMING PROOF.

